pro_course_detail.description:
I like to think of this lesson as being: "Learn to get the words from your brain to your mouth."

If you are like me when I learn another language, I often know what I should say but my mouth just won't work. The only solution I know of is to talk with someone who is patient and will support you as you initially make mistakes and then, over time, build towards fluency.

My teaching strength is in running "goal oriented conversations." Typical things I teach well are:
• Helping you to develop workplace English for your specific job;
• Finding interesting articles to read together and then discuss (we can choose something together);
• Preparing you to pass an interview;
• Giving strong speakers a regular English workout to maintain their English (meaning we essentially become friends talking about what we are doing, our hobbies, our philosophy of life and so on) and;
• Doing role-plays of likely situations as a tourist such as a hotel, restaurant, train station and airport (this is actually a technique I use a lot, typically I find a photograph or illustration of a scene and we use this as a prompt).

Telling me in advance what your goals are will help me prepare and so help us make the most of the first lesson.

Depending on your needs I can correct you more or less. I am happy to help with grammar, pronunciation and tone (perhaps to be more businesslike, scientific or conversational).

I am patient and calm and I find this can bring out the best in most types of learner.

Note that at the end of a lesson I may have to take a 5 minute break so that I can prepare for the next student. You can combine lessons to make longer sessions (for example if you want an hour and a half).

*These are NOT live spoken lessons*

This lesson booking is for the use of my Proofreading and Document Editing services.  Your documents must be written in English.  Whether it's your dissertation, personal statement, business related, article, thesis, novel, etc, that needs checking, correcting and editing, I'm here to help.  You should send me your document in .doc (Word) format.

Please contact me first before booking to confirm your needs. 

